@node Cap01 "Introduction"
  =======================================================================
  V 4.1
  ~~~~~
  Again some people requested that i made the opposite of the Boring ba..
  that are int the S:Operator.cfg. So know you can put the ones that can
  ALWAYS page you, no mather how the CHATFLAG is (ON or OFF) they will 
  override it, and well all is written in your callerslog...just check it
  out. I forgot to mention that in the docs that there are 5 remarks in
  you callerslog. 
 
		1. No Reason, No Chat + Message
                2. Chatflag On        + Message
                3. Chatflag Off       + Message
                4. Override Chatflag  + message  >operator.pw
                5. Boring Bas...      + Message  >operator.cfg

  V 4.2
  ~~~~~
  Little Beta release for the Beta testers..seems fine...but not much
  different, except then for a CTRL-C aborts. :) Forgot about that ..oups

  V 4.3
  ~~~~~
  Hmm here a lot has changed, some bugs that the pager kept paging untill
  the User press CTRL-C, fixed now. Also the Operator.pw has been changed
  into Operator.Always and the Operator.cfg into Operator.Never. Sorry
  about this but otherwise it's getting confusing. :)
  Don't see why i still should make Operator.pw since this is of no use
  with the .Never and .Always :)
  Also added ACP SUPPORT, this will show you when the module is activated
  in the ACP. I suggest EVERYBODY does this coz then it is really nice 
  when your windows are iconified. Now you can see what the user does, 
  besides all the time "MODULE" into acp..

  well that's it for now. If any more ideas, requests, whatever..give me
  a buzz..also if you want personalized doors for you bbs only. :)

 					KeN/LoGiC
  V 4.4
  ~~~~~

  Well for those who know already skip some lines now, for those who are
  not aware of the change, read the PHN.KEN&RYU file on all bbs's spread.
  I won't be typing the same thing twice :-)

  What is new in 4.4. Simple, there was a request from "CENSORED" who 
  asked me if i could include a "REAL LAME DUDE SOLUTION". Well first no-
  body is lame (so that's clear now ain't it!) and secondly, if somebody
  wants something he'll get's it. That's what PHUN is all about no ?
  So 4.4 was born. There is a new file, called S:operator.goodbye
  This ones scans for Handles that will automagically, whether the chat
  is ON or OFF, be logged out. (Who ever wants a thing like this ?) I DO!
  YeK YeK...well anyway, that's it for now folks, as I don't have a new
  suggestion received for further improvements, I think this will be
  enough... Of course, you are always welcome to get your Private Pager
  and to exchange ideas about /X Tools of any kind.

					ChaPLiN/P.H.U.N.

  V 4.5
  ~~~~~

  Oups, Big Bug in there and I didn't notice that since /X versions are
  different ...strange...well fixed now.
  Thx to SnoW/LoGiC for pointing that out!

					ChaPLiN/P.H.U.N.


  V 4.6
  ~~~~~
  Another problem that was reported is that the callerslog missed a 
  returnstring so Amilog couldn't find the logoff time. Didn't look good.
  Thanx to Scorpio for pointing that out to me.
  
  Oki now just for some legal mumbo jumbo. All my tools released and pre-
  released, are free of charge and can always be downloaded FREE at the
  P.H.U.N. Whq...just give it a buzz...and one last thing, yes this is 
  the last P.H.U.N /X Tool released, as future Tools will have the MsT
  /X-DeSiGN Label on them. So next update will be /Y\ystic/X-DeSiGn...


  				   ChaPLiN/P.H.U.N/MsT/X-DeSiGn.
  -EoF-

  =======================================================================
@endnode
@node Cap02 "Requirements"
  =======================================================================
  To install Operator Pager you must have the following things:

    Programm         Location        Description
    ----------       --------        -----------
    Operator.exe     Wherever        Main program
    Operator.always  S:              blacklist file
    Operator.never   S:              Cosysops, friends, etc...
    Operator.goodbye S:              Guess what...

  - an  Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/2000/2500/3000/4000/CDTV/CD³²)
  - the installed Version of OS\2, OS\3 or higher
    (Soft- or Hardware Version)
  - the installed .INFO Files in the directories.
  - AmiExpress v2.xx & v3.xx.

  =======================================================================
@endnode
